 ## Background
-The concept of staged optimization in differentiable rendering originates from the need to handle the ill-posed nature of inverse rendering problems [G]. CoherentGS [S1] introduced a specific schedule for 3D Gaussian splatting to improve sparse view synthesis, using a coarse alignment followed by regularized optimization. Reparameterizing discontinuous integrands for differentiable rendering [S2] proposed a multi-scale approach for mesh-based inverse rendering to avoid local minima in shape and texture reconstruction. These methods build on the differentiability of the volume rendering equation [44-radiance-field-optimization.md].
